## SLURM #SBATCH --job-name compaction (applied by build_slurm_job_name in pythonScriptTemplating.py):
### First Part: e.g. 'job_kdiba_gor01_two_2006-6-12_16-53-46__withNormalCompute'...
# remove 'job_' prefix since that's obvious
# remove 'kdiba_'
# remove 'two_' since that can be determined from just the session name ('2006-6-12_16-53-46')
# → animal_session_name, e.g. 'gor01_2006-6-12_16-53-46'

### Second Part (e.g. `job_suffix`): "_withNormalComputedReplays-qclu_1246789-frateThresh_2.0"
# if '_withNormalComputedReplays', don't include it at all since that's the default
# format 'qclu_' -> 'q'
# format 'frateThresh_2.0' -> 'fr_2'
# Example full name: 'gor01_2006-6-12_16-53-46_q1246789_fr_2_tbin_50ms'


